  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "For TX-0401 (EUR 240.00 to TechMart Online, 20 July 2026), the dispute has been checked and can be filed.\n\n**Reason code:** Since the goods never arrived, the matching code is **goods_not_received**. Earlier I mentioned service_not_rendered, but that code is for services and doesn't fit this case. I've checked eligibility under goods_not_received, and it passed all checks:\n- Reason code: pass\n- Transaction status: pass (settled)\n- Dispute window: pass (90 days, deadline **18 October 2026**)\n- Account restrictions: pass\n\n**Next steps:**\n1. Reply **\"confirm\"** and I'll open the dispute for EUR 240.00 under goods_not_received. This can't be undone, though you can withdraw it later if needed.\n2. Verta's review target is 10 business days for card disputes. You'll get a notification at each status change.\n\nYou also have a second TechMart Online charge of EUR 240.00 on 14 July 2026 (TX-0402). If that was a separate charge for the same purchase, it may qualify as a duplicate charge, and I can check that option too.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with TX-0401 as goods_not_received?",
